                "message": "Keep single-character bytes literals as bytes objects when iterating\n\nIterating over a literal sequence of one-character bytes literals inferred\na C character item type, so the loop variable received integers instead of\nbytes objects.  Single-character str literals still use Py_UCS4, which\nconverts back to str.\n\nThis is a separate change from the mixed sequence item type fix, to allow\nindependent decisions about backports.\n\nCo-authored-by: CommandCodeBot <noreply@commandcode.ai>",
